course: dictionary
lesson: 2017
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one the writer means. The word cone is a good example. «Mum said sorry and bought him a 99 — a cone with a chocolate stick in it.» The 99 and the chocolate stick are clues, so here a cone is something you eat ice cream from.
explain: «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts, but never eat conkers or acorns, because they are poisonous.» Here collect and crafts tell you that a cone is something you pick up from a tree. Pine tells you which kind of cone it is.
explain: Some words describe a shape. «Far to the north lies the biggest forest on land, where snow slides off cone-shaped trees.» The word cone-shaped is a clue: the trees are shaped like a 3D cone, wide at the bottom and pointed at the top. When you meet a word with many meanings, read the whole sentence before you choose one.
fact: A cone can mean a 3D shape, an ice-cream holder, a road marker, a seed case, or a part of your eye.
fact: A 3D cone has one flat circular base that narrows to a point at the top.
fact: An «ice-cream cone» is a crispy holder for ice cream.
fact: A «traffic cone» is an orange or red plastic cone used on roads to mark danger or work areas.
fact: A «pine cone» is the hard, scaly seed case of a pine or fir tree.
exercise: «Mum said sorry and bought him a 99 — a cone with a chocolate stick in it.» What is the cone here? | A seed case from a tree | *A crispy holder for ice cream | A traffic cone for the road | A shape in a maths lesson
exercise: «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts.» What is a pine cone? | *The hard, scaly seed case of a pine tree | A plastic marker on a road | A kind of ice cream | A flat shape with a point
exercise: A cone has one flat circular face, one curved face and one point at the top. What shape is it? | A sphere | A cylinder | A cube | *A cone
test: «Far to the north, snow slides off cone-shaped trees.» What does cone-shaped mean? | Flat like a pancake | *Shaped like a 3D cone, wide at the base and pointed at the top | Round like a ball | Tall and thin like a pole
test: Ava says a cone must always be orange. Is she right? | Cones are always made of ice cream | Yes, every cone is orange | Cones are only found in forests | *No, cone has several meanings, and traffic cones are only one kind
exam: «A real heart is shaped more like a rounded cone with big tubes coming out of the top.» What does cone mean here? | A plastic road marker | A seed case from a tree | *A 3D shape with a round base that narrows to a point | A crispy holder for ice cream
